---
import "../index.css";
---

<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <meta charset="utf-8" />
        <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
        <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" />
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
        <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
        <title>Astro</title>
    </head>
    <body class="flex min-h-screen items-center justify-center p-6 text-center">
        <main class="flex w-full max-w-5xl flex-col items-center gap-4">
            <h1 class="text-5xl">Oscar Byrne's web site</h1>
            <p>on the public inter net</p>
            <h2 class="text-2xl">articles I like</h2>
            <iframe
                class="h-100 w-full border-0"
                allowfullscreen
                src="https://osbyrne.raindrop.page/archive-37288524/embed"
            ></iframe>
            <h2 class="text-2xl">My favorite coding font</h2>
            <a
                class="font-maple-mono text-blue-400 underline-offset-0"
                href="http://font.subf.dev/en/">Maple Mono</a
            >
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <p>2026-07-06</p>
                    <p>
                        I use KeepassXC for all my TOPT, passwords, passkeys
                        along with the Chrome extension. Note that GitHub
                        supports Chrome Password Manager's passkeys, but not
                        KeepassXC's (I havent encountered other cases). I also
                        use the Android KeepassDX, but using is it more
                        difficult. The sync story is worse that Google or Apple
                        ecosystems; I set up Google Drive as backup for the
                        Desktop version and pull a fresh version to my phone
                        from Google Drive when needed
                    </p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>2026-07-06</p>
                    <p>
                        Inspirations for this web site : I Read Borretti's web
                        site (https://borretti.me/) because I learn things or I
                        like the tone or the vibe. I learned a lot trough Near's
                        web site (http://near.blog/).
                    </p>
                </li>
            </ul>
            <h2 class="text-2xl">Projects</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <a class="text-blue-400 underline-offset-0" href="/sponge">
                        Sponge for Google Photos
                    </a>
                </li>
            </ul>
        </main>
    </body>
</html>
